==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Easy to use.
* Low end-lag.
* Slight knockback.
* Surprisingly, both moves can hit [[Sea Beast|Sea Beasts]].

|'''[Z] Quick Tackle'''
* Quick start.
* Decent for extending combos.
* Decent mobility.

|'''[X] Ground Smash'''
* Does a decent knockback to put some distance on [[enemies]] (if the enemy or player doesn’t charge at the user).
* Can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* Quite decent [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Very low startup and endlag.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Very low damage.
* Only two abilities, unlike other fighting styles with three or four abilities.
* Close ranged.
* Slow M1s.
* Vulnerable to teaming.
* Both moves cannot hit regular-sized enemies and players on the ground while using [[Buddha]]'s [[transformation]], due to Buddha's hitbox being positioned above the ground. Only M1s can reliably hit grounded targets while transformed.

|'''[Z] Quick Tackle'''
* Terrible range, and it can't be aimed up or down.
* Doesn't [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].

|'''[X] Ground Smash'''
* Small [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Combat is the only fighting style that only has two moves.
* Combat's moves are similar to the [C] and [X] moves of [[Superhuman]] and [[Godhuman]].
** Its M1s are also similar to [[Superhuman]] and [[Godhuman]], so some players thought that Superhuman is Combat V2 and Godhuman is its V3. However this has been debunked with the release of [[Advanced Combat]].
* Most [[Enemies]] use the M1 of Combat.
* [[Raider]]s use the '''[M1]''' and the '''[Z]''' '''Quick Tackle''' move of Combat.
* Combat has the most realistic idle stance of all [[Fighting Styles]], as it resembles a real-life boxing guard.
* Combat was in Blox Fruits for around 5 whole years without an icon, though an icon has been recently added in [[Updates/29.0|Update 29]].
* After [[Player Profile|Player Profiles]] were added, a new stat was included that shows how many fighting styles a player has mastered out of 12. This includes Combat, meaning that if the player changed their melee before they mastered combat, they cannot get 12/12. But in a later update this was fixed to 11/11.
* This fighting style is used for [[Advanced Combat]]'s puzzle, and it requires beating every [[Awakened Bosses|awakened boss]] with only this.

